{
  "title": "Next.js Commerce \u2014 ecommerce (14,045\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Next.js Commerce\nDomain: ecommerce | Scale: medium | Stars: 14,045\nProblem: Provides a high-performance, production-ready ecommerce template that demonstrates modern Next.js patterns (App Router, React Server Components, Server Actions) while supporting multiple commerce backends through a pluggable provider architecture.\nTarget users: ecommerce merchants, developers building storefronts, Next.js learners, commerce platform providers\nCore features: Multi-provider support (Shopify, BigCommerce, Medusa, Saleor, etc.); Server-rendered product catalog with dynamic revalidation; Shopping cart with Server Actions and useOptimistic updates; Product search with typeahead (via Orama integration); Visual CMS editing (via React Bricks integration); Responsive product details and checkout flow\nIntegrations: Shopify Storefront API, BigCommerce, Medusa, Saleor, Orama (search), React Bricks (CMS)\nTech stack: React 19, Next.js 15 (App Router, Server Components) + Next.js Server Actions, API routes + Vercel\nKey libraries: @headlessui/react, @heroicons/react, tailwindcss, sonner, clsx\nArchitecture: jamstack\nDesign lessons:\n- Pluggable provider architecture decouples commerce backend from presentation layer, enabling multi-platform support with minimal UI changes\n- Heavy use of React Server Components and Server Actions for data fetching and mutations reduces client-side complexity and improves performance\n- Suspense and useOptimistic patterns demonstrate modern Next.js concurrent rendering for optimistic UI updates without request waterfall\n- Template-first approach with integration examples (Orama, React Bricks) shows extensibility patterns for enterprise feature adoption",
